      {
        "id": 127788,
        "name": "Mezike",
        "username": "Mezike",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/c6cbf5/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-16T15:19:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>My family tree is a total clustermess. One strand of the family basically goes back forever in the same few villages in Dorset, mostly farmers until the last century or so when they were mostly shopkeepers. The rest of it is a spaghetti heap of dead ends with Irish, French, Canadian, and a bunch of other influences including some who seem to have existed in the 19th century equivalent of being completely off the grid.</p>\n<p>My kids will have it even harder as my wife's family aren't actually sure about their lineage beyond the last couple of generations, although it's highly likely that the family name came from a Russian soldier who went to Hungary and changed his name to something that sounded a little more Hungarian. Apparently it's a fairly unique surname that is not normal for Hungary but which is used in the Persian region, so there could be an even more convoluted backstory involving a Persian family migrating to Russia and then into Hungary. But there are still more complications that muddy the waters of this part of the story even further, and with so many public records lost, destroyed, or forged during the successive Nazi and Communist occupations nobody really has a scooby about their true geneology. We just like to say that we're starting the family anew from these existing generations  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=9\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\"></p>",
        "post_number": 28,
